    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 1. Setup order\n\n1. **Activate** this workflow, then copy the **Production URL** from the Webhook node. The Test URL only works while the editor is open.\n2. Checkout dashboard -> Developers -> **Webhooks** -> new configuration:\n   - paste that URL\n   - **Generate key** next to *signature key*\n   - subscribe to `payment_captured` (add `payment_declined`, `payment_refunded`, `dispute_received` later)\n3. Put the signature key in the `Verify Signature` node, or better set env `CKO_WEBHOOK_SIGNATURE_KEY`.\n4. Pay a sandbox link from the other workflow and watch the execution.",
        "height": 380,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000014",
      "name": "Note - Setup",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -200,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 2. Signature check\n\nHMAC-SHA256 of the **raw** body with the webhook signature key, compared to the `Cko-Signature` header.\n\nRaw Body must stay ON in the Webhook node. Hashing parsed JSON never matches.\n\nn8n Cloud blocks `$env`, so the key is a literal in the node. Sandbox only: in production put it in a credential.\n\n**`ENFORCE = false` on the first run.** The node reports `signatureValid`, `signatureReceived`, `signatureExpected` and `headerNames` so you can confirm the real header name from a live delivery.\n\nOnce `signatureValid` is true, set `ENFORCE = true`. Until then this URL is an open endpoint that anyone could call.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 2
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000015",
      "name": "Note - Signature",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        260,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 3. What do we do with it?\n\nThe **Mode** node decides:\n\n| mode | effect |\n|---|---|\n| `sheet` | append to a payments log tab only. Nothing touches Xero. |\n| `xero` | find the invoice, guard against duplicates, create the payment, mark the row PAID |\n| `both` | log and post |\n\nStart on **sheet**. It proves the webhook, the signature and the payload with zero accounting risk, and gives Finance a visible list to reconcile by hand.\n\nSwitch to `xero` only once the clearing account code is set and Finance has agreed the posting.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 440,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000016",
      "name": "Note - Mode",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        720,
        -120
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 4. Before mode = xero\n\n- **clearingAccountCode** is `TBD`. Payments book to a **Checkout clearing account**, never straight to the bank: Checkout settles net of fees on a batch, so bank and gross payment never match.\n- **Still Unpaid?** is the idempotency guard. Checkout guarantees at-least-once delivery, so without it a redelivered webhook double-pays the invoice.\n- **Find Invoice in Xero** matches on `Reference`. Today `Post & Send Revenue Invoices` puts the *Checkout link* in Reference, so the payment `reference` must carry the same value, or this query has to change.\n- Partial payments are not handled: the guard is `AmountDue > 0`, and the full amount is posted.",
        "height": 420,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 3
      },
      "id": "b1000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000017",
      "name": "Note - Xero branch",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1240,
        700
      ]
    }
